🚀 Day 4 — GCP IAM + Service Accounts + Security

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your organization has 50+ GCP projects across multiple teams. How will you design IAM (org, folders, projects, groups, roles) to follow least privilege and still keep management simple?

2️⃣ A service account key used in production is accidentally pushed to a public Git repo. What immediate and long-term actions will you take in GCP to secure the environment?

3️⃣ You have separate dev, QA, and prod projects. An application needs access to Cloud Storage and Cloud SQL in each. How will you design IAM so developers don’t get prod-level permissions, but the app still works end-to-end?

4️⃣ Security has mandated: “No public IPs for VMs and only specific regions allowed.” How will you enforce this using IAM & Organization Policies across all current and future projects?

5️⃣ Your GKE workloads currently use JSON keys to access GCP APIs. How will you redesign this to remove keys and implement secure, short-lived credentials using Workload Identity?

6️⃣ A Cloud Storage bucket with customer data was accidentally made public. How will you lock it down, verify current exposure, and prevent such misconfigurations in future?

7️⃣ One project runs a backend API, another project hosts data in BigQuery and Cloud Storage. How will you design cross-project access using IAM without sharing keys or over-granting roles?

8️⃣ Your company onboards and offboards engineers frequently. What IAM model (groups, custom roles, folders, policies) will you use so access can be adjusted with minimal manual effort and low risk?

9️⃣ A Cloud Build pipeline fails with “PERMISSION_DENIED” when deploying to GKE and updating secrets. How will you systematically troubleshoot and fix IAM for the Cloud Build service account?

🔟 You want to allow SSH/RDP access to VMs only for specific admins, without public IPs on the VMs. How will you combine IAM, IAP, and OS Login to achieve this?

1️⃣1️⃣ Your security team wants visibility into all high-risk IAM changes (role grants, policy updates). How will you design logging, alerting, and review workflows in GCP?

1️⃣2️⃣ Sensitive data must be encrypted with customer-managed keys (CMEK) and keys must be rotated regularly. How will you design KMS, IAM for key usage, and key rotation strategy?

1️⃣3️⃣ You are building a multi-tenant SaaS on GCP. How will you use projects, folders, IAM, and possibly VPC-SC to isolate tenants while keeping operations manageable?

1️⃣4️⃣ A Cloud Run service should only read one specific secret and one specific Cloud SQL instance. How will you design service accounts, IAM roles, and bindings to enforce this strictly?
